values ('ap_statistics', 3, '3.3', array['3.3', '3.5']::text[], 'convention', 'Identify the procedure and parameter for one proportion', 'The procedure for a confidence interval for one population proportion is a one-sample z-interval, and the parameter must name the proportion, the response variable, and the population in context.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Define the parameter in words with the population from the problem. A bare symbol like p is not enough. For a hypothesis test the procedure is a one-sample z-test, and the parameter is described the same way.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-statistics-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_statistics-u3-r2-004; ced=3.3.A.1 "one-sample z-interval for a population proportion"; 3.3.A.2 "reference the proportion, the response variable, and the population in context"')
