values ('ap_statistics', 3, '3.7', array['3.7', '3.13', '3.15']::text[], 'convention', 'Conclusion wording for a hypothesis test', 'State the conclusion in context, consistent with and in terms of the alternative hypothesis, using non-definitive language. A one-proportion test conclusion refers to the parameter and the population (3.7.B.6); a two-proportion test conclusion refers to the parameters and the populations (3.13.C.3); a chi-square test conclusion refers to the population(s) (3.15.D.3).', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Never say "accept" or "prove" the null hypothesis. A large p-value means there is not convincing evidence for the alternative, which is different from evidence for the null. For chi-square tests, say the data do not provide convincing evidence of an association or a difference, rather than saying there is none.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-statistics-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_statistics-u3-r3-002; ced=3.7.B.6 "stated in context consistent with, and in terms of, the alternative hypothesis using non-definitive language"; 3.7.B.4; 3.13.C.3; 3.15.D.3; product-owner-directed correction by the Claude session (David, 2026-10-10): the escalated row was corrected against its own CED evidence and re-checked by both independent checkers and the own-family veto')
